Conclusions
We investigated the existence of non-perturbative effects in spin glasses with a Monte Carlo (MC) study for an Ising spin glass in a field where pairwise couplings are disposed in a hierarchical waythe hierarchical Edwards-Anderson model in a magnetic field (HEA). The spin-interaction decay in the HEA is controlled by the parameter s, which is reminiscent of the dimension d for a ferromagnetic Ising model28: in particular, the mean-field (MF) and nonmean-field (NMF) regions s # 2/3 and s . 2/3 correspond to d $ 4 and d , 4 respectively19. The HEA is suitable for assessing the existence of non-perturbative effects for two reasons: First, the binary nature of couplings and magnetic fields makes the HEA fit for non-perturbative numerical approaches, such as MC simulations26. Second, the hierarchical structure of the couplings reproduces the
