the other hand, our findings show that the phase transition in the NMF region cannot be captured by an approach where corrections to the MF picture are considered as a perturbation. This fact raises the possibility that the physical features of this transition are markedly different from the MF ones: this possibility is reminiscent of scenarios alternative to the RSB one, such as the droplet picture13 or other scenarios intermediate between the RSB and the droplet one29. In this regard, the structure of the low-lying energy states could be directly analyzed by probing the low-energy excitations above the ground state29,30 and by characterizing, for example, their stiffness31 and surface dimension32. A interesting possibility would then be to study how the resulting picture for the low-energy landscape relates to the existence of non-perturbative effects. Taken together, the points above provide an interesting direction that is worth exploring in future studies.
